# Cross-Tool CLI Dispatch

This machine has three AI coding tools installed. Each can invoke the others
non-interactively via CLI. **When the user asks you to use another tool
(e.g. "让 claude review 一下", "用 codex 去审查"), invoke it directly via shell.
Do NOT refuse or suggest the user copy-paste manually.**

## Available CLIs (from Cursor's perspective)

| Tool | Command | Output |
|------|---------|--------|
| Claude Code | `claude -p "<prompt>" --allowedTools "Read Glob Grep" > out.md` | stdout |
| Codex | `codex exec -o out.md "<prompt>"` | `-o` flag |
| Codex review | `codex review --base main "<prompt>"` | stdout |
| Cursor (self) | N/A (you are Cursor) | — |

## Usage example

```bash
# Ask Claude Code to review a feature
claude -p "Review packages/plugin-organizer/ for architecture compliance" \
  --allowedTools "Read Glob Grep" > docs/reviews/organizer/claude-review.md

# Ask Codex to review branch changes
codex review --base main "Review for correctness, edge cases, and missing error handling"
```

## Rules

1. Write output to `docs/reviews/<feature>/` for traceability
2. The dispatched tool reads the same repo; no extra context needed
3. Background dispatch (`&`) is fine for batch operations
4. Cross-reference: `docs/workflow/_portable/04-automation-loop.md` for advanced patterns

